      "group": "overview",
      "content": "Cross-section comparison of 10 global banks across the **Banks - Global** industry — four US money-centers (BAC, C, JPM), two Canadian banks (BMO, TD), three European banks (BCS, DB, HSBC, UBS) and one Indian-banked ADR (IBN). They span P/Es from 9.79 (DB) to 20.11 (TD), and YTD performance from -3.11% (DB) to +43.15% (BMO). Today's tape is broadly defensive: **8 of 10 are red**, led by UBS -2.85% and C -2.36%; only HSBC (+0.06%) and IBN (+0.58%) sit flat-to-up. Combined reported total assets reach ~**$2,690B**, dominated by JPM's $922.16B. Across the group, **7 of 10 carry Buy consensus**, all 10 trade at sub-21x trailing P/E, and **8 of 10 are within 5% of their 52-week highs** — a signal of broad sector strength heading into the next catalyst window."
